I return to the apartment from the clinic.
I am very tired.
I walk slowly through the hallway.
Then my neighbor Anitha opens her door.
She looks at my face.
"Maya, aren't you feeling well?" Anitha asks.
"Yes, I feel really unwell," I reply.
"I have a bad fever and cold."
"My head and throat are hurting."
Anitha feels concerned.
"You must go to the room and lie down now," she says.
"You must rest well."
I nod my head.
"I will bring some hot kanji for you for lunch," Anitha says.
I feel very relieved.
"Thank you very much, Anitha," I say.
I open the door to my flat.
I quickly go to the bedroom.
